English Version / 英文版本
=========================

This repository is a **derivative work** (secondary development) of
**walksQAQ/Wows_Paragrams_Unpack**. It is not an official fork and does not
represent the original author. Major changes from upstream: removed the GUI /
D3D11 renderer / data-browsing features, rewrote the GLB export and geometry
assembly pipeline, redesigned the database (single-version mirror +
incremental sync), and added armor export, manifest, and quantization modules.

Portions created by walksQAQ remain copyright walksQAQ.
Portions added or modified in this repository remain copyright their author.
Both are licensed under the terms below.

1. **Apache License 2.0**: All code and documentation in this repository
   (including upstream portions and this repository's modifications), EXCEPT
   the files listed in items 2 and 3 below, are licensed under the Apache
   License, Version 2.0. See LICENSE.Apache-2.0.

2. **GNU General Public License v3.0 or later**: `data_extractor/kraken.py`
   is a port based on domdfcoding/kraken-decompressor (GPLv3) and is
   licensed solely under the GPLv3, not Apache-2.0. See LICENSE.GPLv3
   and the license notice in the file header.

3. **MIT License**: The four files in `uncode_assets/` ported from
   https://github.com/landaire/wows-toolkit (`parser.py`, `vfs.py`,
   `binary.py`, `decoders.py`) retain upstream's MIT license,
   copyright Lander Brandt. See LICENSE.MIT for the full text and the
   file mapping. MIT is compatible with Apache-2.0 and may be distributed
   together with the rest of this repository.

**Combined distribution notice (important)**: `data_extractor/kraken.py`
is imported by the rest of this program and forms a single combined work.
Under the GPLv3 copyleft, when you **distribute** the combined program
(e.g., a packaged executable), the distribution as a whole must comply
with the corresponding GPLv3 obligations (providing corresponding source,
etc.). Apache-2.0 is GPL-compatible and may coexist with GPLv3 in the
same program; the above constraint applies only when you distribute the
combined work, and does not affect your freedom to use or modify the
Apache-2.0-licensed portions on their own.

